WEBVTT

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.470
Morning!

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:32.490
Morning.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.490
Hey, did you see last night's TV drama?

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:36.960
First period is English, right?

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.240
A new card?

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.850
Yeah.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:44.760
And...

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.680
A key, too.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.630
It's see-through...

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.170
But when you turn it over,

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.510
the print on the other side doesn't show through.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.030
The cards from before suddenly turned clear.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.380
And now you get a new card.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.480
So many strange things keep happening...

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:11.140
But there's a far more
important issue at hand.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.380
What is it?

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:18.510
I didn't get to film your
first new card capture!

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.570
<b>Whimper</b>

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:23.890
And I... And I had a new 
outfit all ready for you!

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.600
What about mine?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.870
<b>You said you had a 
stock of them, but you 
still made a new one...</b>

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.870
Of course!

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.550
There, you go.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.210
Yay!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:35.260
Yay! Yay! Yay!

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.520
Daidouji really hasn't changed at all, huh?

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.460
No.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.510
Yay! Yay!

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.510
Still, I'm so glad you weren't hurt.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.940
Yeah. Thanks.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.500
What do you think, Syaoran-kun?

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.280
I don't sense any power in them but yours.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.640
Me, either.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:02.060
But why are these things 
happening in Tomoeda again?

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.920
We'll talk again later, okay?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:11.960
Sure.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:16.850
Sakura...

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:23.970
<b>Sakura and the Room with No Exit</b>

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.620
Morning!

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:28.810
Morning.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.720
Good morning.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:34.180
Whew, good. The teacher isn't here yet.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.320
Morning, Sakura-chan. Tomoyo-chan.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.990
Morning, Chiharu-chan.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.520
Good morning.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.700
<b>Rare Cheesecake Recipe</b>

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.700
Here's my cheesecake recipe.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.200
Thanks!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.330
It's just how I personally make it...

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.320
Your cheesecake was really good, 
so I wanted to learn to make it.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.600
The fruit sauce was exquisite, as well.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.880
Tomoyo-chan and I will try making it today.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.640
Let me know what you think of it.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:03.360
Sure!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.730
Good morning!

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:08.220
Take your seats.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.840
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:09.840
See you later.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.990
<i>If it comes out good, 
I'll share it with everyone.</i>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.080
<i>Including Syaoran-kun.</i>

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.740
<b>Club Application Form 

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:23.740
Now...

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:28.430
You're all supposed to turn in your club 
applications by the end of the week.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.390
Have you all decided on a club?

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:32.320
Have you decided yet?

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.840
Which one are you joining?

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.250
Have you decided, Sakura-chan?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.090
Yeah. Have you?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.960
I'm thinking of joining the Chorus 
Club, like in elementary school.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.580
Same here! I'm going for cheerleading!

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.830
I wonder if Chiharu-chan will, too.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.970
Let's ask her later.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:51.900
Which club do you think Li-kun will join?

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.090
I'm not sure...

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:57.150
He wasn't in any clubs before.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:01.800
I hope he'll find a way to enjoy 
his after-school time, too.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.740
Yeah.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.510
If he joins an athletic club,

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:08.130
the Cheerleading Club would 
go and cheer for him.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:14.040
And if I could film you doing 
that, I'd be so happy!

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.030
I'm going for cheerleading, too.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:21.040
So we'll be together again.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.100
Yeah! Can't wait!

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.330
I decided to join the Drama Club.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:30.290
The Tomoeda Middle School Drama Club 
also performs plays written by students.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.590
The script you wrote for our play 
in elementary school was great.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.510
I would love to see the club 
put on one of your plays.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:40.520
I'll be rooting for you, too.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:41.880
Thanks!

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.700
What about you, Yamazaki-kun?

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.090
The Basketball Club scouted me.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.870
Yeah, you're definitely tall, if nothing else!

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:54.170
But if we'd had a Rakugo Society, 
I would've liked to join it.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.560
Well, we don't.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:59.570
Which is why I thought I'd join the Lacrosse Club!

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:05.340
<b>Smack</b>

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.960
That has nothing to do with anything!

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:06.920
What about you, Li-kun?

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.730
I don't plan to join any clubs.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.390
You don't?

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.960
I only just got back from Hong Kong...

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.850
I have a lot of things I need to do.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.180
Things you need to do?

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:26.440
Like, a lot of paperwork, 
and things I need to get together.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.990
I hope you can join a club, 
once you finish all that.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.740
Yeah, that'd be nice.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.050
Did Wei-san come back with you?

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:40.710
No, just me.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.000
But he said he'd come
to check on me in a while.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.640
What about Meiling-chan?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.580
You exchange messages with her all the time.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.130
You'd probably know better than me.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:54.890
Yes, she always sends
us fun pictures and videos.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:58.920
The outfit she wore for that festival 
a while ago was adorable!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.530
Yeah, it was so cute!

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.320
I used it as a reference.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.040
That outfit?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.740
I'm sure it will look wonderful on you!

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:11.540
You weren't in the picture 
with her, though, Li-kun.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.600
Yeah...

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.650
I had something else to do that day,

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.340
so I didn't go to the festival.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:21.420
I see...

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.420
I wish I could have used it as a reference.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.200
For what?

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.530
To make something that would 
look wonderful on you!

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:30.550
Speaking of festivals...

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.730
There are many different 
festivals around the world,

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.820
but a particularly uncommon 
one is found in Bulgaria.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.960
It involves yogurt and salted fish guts—

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.190
Here. Eat faster.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.930
Lunch break is almost over!

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:45.900
Yum.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.510
I wanted to hear the rest!

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.210
It's the same for Li-kun,

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:53.440
but I hope Sakura-chan never changes, either.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.450
<b>Art Room</b>

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:01.690
How's it going?

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.950
It's so hard.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.210
I bet Naoko-chan would have 
no problem with this...

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:15.610
Naoko-chan really is good at drawing.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:17.140
Can I see?

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.090
S-Sure.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.890
Hey, it looks really nice!

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.280
Y-You think so?

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.330
It's very good.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:31.010
Hearing that from someone as good as 
you are is embarrassing, Tomoyo-chan.

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:36.330
No, both of your drawings look lovely!

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.900
Yeah. And yours looks really 
sophisticated, somehow.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:43.160
Thank you.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:45.560
I'm unsure how I feel about it myself.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.920
It's like the design illustrations 
we looked at before!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.920
When I make outfits, 
I always draw designs first.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.880
You draw them before you make them?

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:58.930
Sometimes, I draw them 
directly onto pattern paper.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:03.430
But I always draw the ideas I come 
up with, so I won't forget them.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.420
That's amazing!

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:07.480
Next time we have Home Ec.,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.500
can you teach me the sewing 
stuff I can't figure out?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.330
Of course.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:14.310
Thanks!

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:28.140
Li-kun really is athletic, huh?

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.250
Y-Yeah, he is.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.080
I hope he's able to join a club soon.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:36.780
Definitely.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:41.080
Is this right?

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:46.070
Yeah, that should be fine.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.700
Everything looks good here, too.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:53.330
Let's see... According to the recipe 
Chiharu-chan wrote for us...

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:54.900
<b>Rare Cheesecake Recipe</b>

00:09:55.860 --> 00:10:00.530
Place cream cheese in a bowl, 
and stir until smooth.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:02.460
So, like this.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.550
And this!

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.500
Add sugar to whipping cream.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.790
It might be a good idea to add honey, too.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:13.920
When the mixture forms soft peaks, 
add the cream cheese,

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.380
along with lemon juice.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.330
Like this?

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:19.100
And then like this, right?

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:20.060
Here!

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:24.310
Place gelatin powder in a heat-resistant 
bowl and microwave it.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.850
Then add the melted gelatin to the mixture.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:28.440
Like this.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:32.000
Pass the mixture through a sieve, 
and then pour it into the pan.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:32.810
Like this!

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:36.730
Then let it set in the refrigerator 
for two to three hours.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:37.810
Like this!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:42.500
Top it with fresh fruit, mint, 
or fruit sauce, as desired,

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.610
and enjoy!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.820
The rare cheesecake...

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:49.340
is done!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.040
<b>Banzai!</b>

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.270
<b>Ahhh!</b>

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:10.980
Oh, my!

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:14.860
Chiharu-chan's recipes never 
disappoint. It's fantastic!

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:19.980
Ah... Happiness is eatin' tasty foods!

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:27.330
Yeah.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:30.400
I definitely agree.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.870
With the new staff and card,

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:38.090
and the fact that Eriol-kun 
hasn't replied to me yet,

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.420
I've had a lot on my mind.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:43.040
But spending all my time worrying won't help.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.550
At school and at home,

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:47.340
I'll just do what I have to do every day.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:51.050
And if anything happens, 
I'll do whatever I can.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.460
You're so amazing, Sakura-chan.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:02.350
No, not at all!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.930
That's right...

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:08.150
Even in middle school, you still turn off 
your alarm and go back to sleep,

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:11.140
and then have to rush to get ready...

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:12.370
Kero-chan!

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:13.610
Oh, my!

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:15.870
I'm home.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.500
Onii-chan...

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.130
Welcome home.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:20.870
Thanks.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.260
Yukito-san!

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.510
Hi, Sakura-chan and Tomoyo-chan.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.280
I hope I'm not intruding.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.640
<b>Pretending He's a Plushie</b>

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.610
So you're staying over tonight, Tomoyo-chan?

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:42.400
Yes, I'll be spending the night!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.790
I am, too.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:45.500
You're spending the night, too?

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.730
Yeah. Hope you don't mind.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.620
No, it's great to have you!

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.090
What does that mean?

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.330
What?

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.600
"Great to have him," so you can do what?

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:58.660
S-So I can show him my hospitality!

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.180
Yeah? How?

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.110
W-Well...

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:08.770
Just hearing you say that is hospitality 
enough for me, Sakura-chan.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.810
Yukito-san!

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.060
It's a shame I don't have
my camcorder with me.

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:17.260
<i>Typical Tomoyo...</i>

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:23.440
Is okonomiyaki okay for dinner?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.440
I love okonomiyaki!

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.320
So do I.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.700
We have soba, too, so I'll make modan-yaki.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.960
<i>Modan-yaki!</i>

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:37.690
Ke—

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:38.960
Ke?

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:43.460
Ke... Key to good health! 
That's modan-yaki!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.060
Good health?

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:48.340
Y-Yeah, since it has lots of cabbage...

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.690
Not bad, I guess.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.850
And after I set some aside, just for you!

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:08.980
Now, you can't have any!

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.660
Onii-chan!

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:16.390
What are you doing?

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.050
They're so close.

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.800
They sure are.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:17.790
It's not bad.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:22.000
<i>Guys... Stayin' a plushie
for this long ain't easy!</i>

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:27.970
Ugh... Even after starting college, 
he's such a meanie!

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:34.560
He sure makes a tasty okonomiyaki, 
though. He can't be all bad.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.770
You're just a glutton, Kero-chan.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:41.520
Anyone who can make
tasty food is a good person.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:48.910
It's the perfect length!

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.070
I haven't worn anything
like this in a long time.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.350
It looks great on you.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:02.610
Wearing the outfits you make for me 
always gives me lots of energy.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.000
Thanks for always doing this.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.380
Sakura-chan...

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.390
Now, to mark the occasion with a video!

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:15.820
Of course you have to film it, huh?

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:17.270
I'm in!

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:20.160
You look so cute! Beautiful!

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:22.730
Something just...

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:25.320
What's goin' on?

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:30.570
I thought we were just in Sakura-chan's room.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:34.340
Y-Yeah, we were... right?

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.790
Is this... another dream?

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:54.010
<b>Tug</b>

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:54.010
Ow!

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.230
How's that?

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.990
It hurts, Kero-chan!

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:57.780
Ow!

00:15:58.650 --> 00:15:59.870
Which means...

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.030
It's not a dream?

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:05.500
Then...

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.970
It has something to do with
my new staff and card?

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.530
Sure seems that way.

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:24.190
What is this place?

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:30.970
Again... I don't sense anything.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.720
Is there a door, somewhere?

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:38.470
Be careful.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:40.920
I will.

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:45.980
Well?

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:49.290
I don't sense anything, either.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:53.790
Huh?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:55.430
What is it?

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.010
The wall is running from me!

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:08.890
What the heck is this?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.380
No doors or windows.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.790
When pushed, it stretches away.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.760
How do we get out?

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.740
S-Seriously...

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:48.950
What's the deal with these walls?!

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:53.310
What now?

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:58.850
Tomoyo-chan!

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:02.850
Sakura-chan!

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:05.410
What's goin' on?

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.110
What is this? It's all flimsy.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.610
I know what this is! It's...

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.710
It's... You know! It's... that!

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:19.490
What?

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.750
It's that! <i>That</i>!

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:23.910
I don't know what "that" is!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.880
That stuff! It stretches, then contracts!

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:28.010
You know!

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:32.080
Rubber!

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:37.430
Is this something like being inside a balloon?

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.590
That might be it!

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.380
Then, if we could pop it, maybe...

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.610
But how?

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.970
I just happen to have these.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:56.420
Right.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.490
<i>Key that hides the forces of dreams!</i>

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.930
<i>Show me your true form!</i>

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.510
<i>Release!</i>

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:24.730
Here I go.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:25.600
Okay.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:35.180
Sakura!

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:35.890
Right.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.880
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:41.760
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:45.420
<i>Secure!</i>

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:09.670
Siege... The Siege card.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.140
I heard a really loud noise.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:22.200
W-We were just playing with 
a balloon, and it popped.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:24.150
We're sorry.

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.160
Don't get too wild in here.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:29.780
O-Okay.

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:37.040
We managed to keep him in the dark...

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:40.410
Sakura?

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:44.350
Another new card...

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.720
Ruby is asleep.

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.230
She kept insisting on going
to Japan right away.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.180
Kaho finally calmed her down.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:03.610
I see.

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:08.900
You're not going to call the girl in Japan?

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:13.080
Isn't she waiting for your reply, Eriol?

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:15.910
No, not yet.

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:19.430
Not until the right time comes.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:40.750
No!

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.230
No! Not that way!

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.870
No! You can't go!

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:49.880
Who are you? Why are you there?

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:51.730
Who...

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:53.430
are you?

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:08.620
<i>They're still clear.</i>

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:11.680
<i>I hope the cards are all right.</i>

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:19.350
Modan-yaki's gotta have pork and squid...

00:22:23.180 --> 00:22:24.840
<i>I'll do what I can.</i>

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:32.120
<i>There must be a reason why I encountered 
these new cards, after all.</i>

00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:35.140
<i>I'll do anything I can</i>

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:38.170
<i>so that I can see all the cards again.</i>

00:24:10.460 --> 00:24:12.710
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.980
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.980
<b>K</b>

00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:13.760
Yo!

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:16.480
The "Leave It to Kero-chan!" segment has begun,

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:18.850
and the first installment is all about this!

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:21.440
The Tomoeda Middle School uniform!

00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:23.710
Black is the base color of its chic design,

00:24:23.710 --> 00:24:25.560
and the red lines create a focal point.

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:29.400
The insignia on the left shoulder is 
the same as Tomoeda Elementary's!

00:24:29.710 --> 00:24:31.490
By the way, this is the boys' uniform.

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:32.490
<b>Describe the boys', too! 

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:39.040
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:39.040
<b>K</b>

00:24:32.830 --> 00:24:36.700
I'll be bringing you all kinds of info in this 
segment every week, just like this,

00:24:36.700 --> 00:24:38.360
so don't miss it!

00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.540
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.320 --> 00:24:43.050
I submitted my application 
to the Cheerleading Club!

00:24:43.050 --> 00:24:44.550
I'm so excited!

00:24:44.550 --> 00:24:46.830
But the rain won't stop...

00:24:46.830 --> 00:24:48.910
Could this be the work of a card?

00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:51.780
Next time, "Sakura's Heavy Rain Alert."

00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura's Heavy Rain Alert</b>

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:54.550
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
